WEBVTT

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:05.950
<i>Currently, we are in a survival situation.</i>

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:11.190
<b>Our First Meal</b>

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:11.280
<i>It seems this place... is a deserted island.</i>

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:18.800
<i>In search of water, we entered the forest.</i>

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:29.710
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:32.510
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:26.140
I'm sorry, Shion-san.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:28.480
It's all right. Just rest.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:32.940
Still, I wonder why we have
to go looking for trash.

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:36.480
That Onishima girl...
Somehow, I just don't trust her.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:40.460
But she knows a lot.
And she fought off a shark for us.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:42.030
She seems dependable.

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:45.060
It feels like talking with a grown up.

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:49.110
I'm way more dependable than she—

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:53.170
It looks uncomfortable,
lying on the ground like that...

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:54.060
Huh?

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:57.300
Just a minute, okay? I'll go find something.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:58.090
U-Um...

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:04.620
I feel like we were supposed
to find something to hold water...

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:12.750
Hey, Homare!

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:14.690
Don't just keep forging ahead.

00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:17.510
We should rest a little.

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:19.070
I'm fine.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:22.590
You don't have to come with me.

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:24.410
Wh-What?

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.440
I'll be fine on my own.

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:31.960
You know... You could be a little friendlier...

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:34.710
Calling me "you." It's Asuka.

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:36.670
A-su-ka.

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:39.660
We all introduced ourselves already, right?

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:41.460
It's a wasp.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:42.550
No, a sawfly.

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:44.720
She's not listening.

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:47.520
They don't fly far from their nests.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.620
There should be a water source
within a few kilometers of here.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.190
Hey! Are we going already?

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:55.070
Hey, wait for me!

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:58.050
A few kilometers, huh?

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:04.830
Huh?

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:09.270
I found something!

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:12.880
<b>Strain
Strain
Strain
Strain</b>

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:11.810
Here! You can use it as a pillow!

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:13.400
Sh-Sh-Shion-san?

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:16.050
Wait... That... Isn't that a coconut?

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:17.630
It can't be.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:20.050
It isn't like any coconut I've seen.

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:24.640
When I was little, I had one in Hawaii
and it was a lot greener.

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:28.490
It probably drifted here.

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:31.700
Homare-san said there weren't
any coconut trees on this island.

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.610
Wait... If that's true then...

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:36.150
Huh?

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:42.320
The coconut I had back then was so full
of juice I couldn't finish it on my own.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:47.430
L-Let's share it with everyone, Shion-san.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:51.160
O-Of course I'd let you have
some first, Amatani-san.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:53.880
Oh, thank you.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:54.580
Huh?

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.670
<b>Praise me. Say I did good. Praise me. Praise me.</b>

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:05.270
You're such a help! Shion-san, I owe you my life!

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:08.050
Don't be silly. It's not a big deal.

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:13.440
<i>She's kind of a lot of work, this Shion-san.</i>

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:16.440
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:15.870
Really?

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:19.150
I'm tired!

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:21.550
It should be near here, but...

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:26.350
We walked a ton 
and there's no water anywhere!

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:31.600
There're signs that water flowed through here.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:34.390
When it rains, this must become a stream.

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:36.650
Rain, huh?

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:38.750
Let's try digging.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:43.840
There's often water
flowing beneath riverbeds.

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:46.260
Seriously?

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:52.580
<i>This is bad. I'm getting lightheaded.</i>

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:54.020
<i>I might be done for.</i>

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:58.520
Hey. Open your mouth.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.570
Huh? What's that supposed to be?

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:04.150
There wasn't any water, but the soil is very damp.

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:07.180
W-Water?

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:08.030
More!

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:12.180
If you wrap damp soil in cloth
like this and suck on it,

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:13.840
you can wring out the water.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:18.630
It's so good! It's the best water
I've had in my whole life!

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:23.120
Really, we should boil it first,
but this is an emergency.

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:25.130
So good! I want another!

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:29.730
Sorry... I know you're thirsty, too...

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:31.740
You should drink next, Homare!

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:32.390
Huh?

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:35.650
You can keep using that.

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:36.640
But...

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:39.730
I have another sock, after all.

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:42.100
Huh?

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:45.090
So good!

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:49.770
At least let me use my own sock!

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:51.370
As you like.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:54.370
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:54.370
Really?

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:59.360
I'm sorry for getting your hopes up.

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:02.850
I wanted you to be able
to drink it, Amatani-san.

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:06.020
You don't need to apologize, Shion-san.

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:13.850
Plus... it took a lot of energy to break
the coconut open, didn't it, Shion-san?

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:19.100
I have a favor to ask. Will you listen?

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:19.810
Huh?

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:23.740
I want you to answer "yes," but...

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:29.480
If by chance... I manage to pee...

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:30.990
Huh?

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:34.970
I want you to drink it.

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:39.840
...because I want you to live...

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:41.920
Shion... san...

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:45.670
Please... say you will...

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:50.000
I will!

00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:58.400
Rain!

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:01.600
Look!

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:06.010
Blessed rain is falling from
the heavens, just for you!

00:07:06.870 --> 00:07:08.160
Shion-san...

00:07:08.890 --> 00:07:10.070
...your underwear...

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:16.580
This is the best water
I've had in my whole life!

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:19.160
Ah, such blessed rain!

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.150
<i>I feel like she's said that before.</i>

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:22.170
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:22.170
Really?

00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:25.830
So, we've managed to secure water for now.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:28.170
About what we need next...

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:32.090
In survival situations,
there are three rules of three.

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:34.020
First:

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:36.880
If a person is unable to maintain
proper body temperature,

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:38.350
they die within three hours.

00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:39.950
Second:

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:42.940
Without water, a person
can only live three days.

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:44.700
Third:

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:47.120
Without food, a person dies in three weeks.

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:51.490
The thing we must prepare
as soon as possible is...

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:54.140
a shelter with a roof to preserve
our body temperatures.

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:56.470
Man, I'm starving...

00:07:56.470 --> 00:07:59.500
Me, too. I'm so hungry
I don't think I can move.

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:02.160
We haven't eaten anything in forever.

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:06.000
We're all at our limit here. Shelter?

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.670
Can you eat that?

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:10.580
If you've got food, you'll survive somehow!

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:11.830
You're all going to die.

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:13.280
Wh-What'd you say?

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:14.590
But, I suppose...

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:16.550
If you insist, then I have no choice.

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:25.600
<b>buzz
buzz
buzz
buzz</b>

00:08:24.510 --> 00:08:25.820
Today's meal.

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:27.110
<b>cicadas         buzz
buzz
buzz
buzz</b>

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:27.690
Mysterious jar

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:27.690
Sea urchin

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:27.690
<b>cicadas         buzz
buzz
buzz
Seaweed</b>

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:38.990
buzz buzz buzz buzz

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:31.860
My hunger has decreased dramatically.

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:33.260
What's in that jar?

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:35.520
The sea urchin's the only
thing that seems edible...

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:38.990
Okay. Let's be fair and do rock-paper-scissors.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:40.640
The winner picks first!

00:08:40.980 --> 00:08:44.470
Nutritionally, wouldn't it be
better to split everything?

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:46.290
<i>Nutritionally?</i>

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:47.900
Ready, and...

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:49.340
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:50.910
Yay!

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:52.670
Sorry! I'm taking the sea urchin!

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:55.930
But, how do you eat this?

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:57.780
You break the outside.

00:08:57.780 --> 00:08:58.720
I'll do it.

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:02.020
There.

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:04.770
The edible parts are the yellow egg sacs.

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:07.560
Dispose of the rest and rinse it in seawater.

00:09:07.950 --> 00:09:10.970
It looks the same as what they sell in stores.

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:13.780
It's so sweet!

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:15.870
This is delicious, Onishima-san!

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:16.660
I'm glad.

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:18.540
Can't you get some more?

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:19.550
More?

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:21.990
buzz buzz buzz buzz

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:21.990
<i>The only thing that looks
decent is the seaweed.</i>

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:24.170
<i>This is my last chance!</i>

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:25.580
Ready, and...

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:26.890
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:30.090
I'm sorry. I'll take this one.

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:33.970
Can you really eat that?

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:37.090
Any green or brown sea weed is edible.

00:09:37.350 --> 00:09:38.810
And the nutritional value is decent.

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:42.600
How is it?

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:47.550
It's a little salty and tough, but it's edible.

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:50.110
Could it be wakame?

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:51.710
Yes.

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:54.690
Just like with wild herbs, wakame
is tough if not harvested in the spring.

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:57.530
All that's left is the cicadas and the jar?

00:09:57.530 --> 00:10:00.590
I'm fine with either, so you can pick.

00:10:00.590 --> 00:10:02.200
Really? Then...

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:04.620
buzz buzz buzz buzz

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:07.330
Then I'm putting my bets on this jar!

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:13.450
Now that I look closer... isn't this jam?

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:16.550
You're right. It looks like blueberry jam...

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:18.530
Awesome! I picked a winner!

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:21.320
But you should still check
the smell and things...

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:20.800
Thanks for the food!

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:27.100
I guess it was rotten...

00:10:27.420 --> 00:10:29.030
Only the cicadas are left.

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:33.010
Among those who eat insects,
cicadas are popular.

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:35.190
buzz buzz buzz buzz

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.190
And you can catch them with your bare hands.

00:10:35.620 --> 00:10:38.400
After plucking off a wing so it can't get away,

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:39.810
you pull off the head.

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:44.920
Cicadas have muscles that control
the wings near the head juncture.

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:48.930
Delicious.

00:10:49.530 --> 00:10:51.830
It tastes like shrimp,
so you can even eat it raw.

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:52.920
Sh-Shrimp?

00:10:56.770 --> 00:10:59.350
But it's still a cicada...

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:00.530
I can't...

00:11:00.530 --> 00:11:02.930
Asuka-san. You can eat wakame with me.

00:11:03.380 --> 00:11:05.190
Thank you...

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:06.290
It really is good, though...

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:07.280
Shrimp?

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:14.080
Sunset.

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:15.660
We'll sleep on the beach today.

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:16.820
What?

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:18.880
It'll be cold at night, won't it?

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:21.740
That's why I suggested making a shelter.

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:24.030
Yeah, but...

00:11:28.690 --> 00:11:30.250
You've gotta be kidding me.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:31.330
She's already asleep.

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:34.220
It's amazing she's dead
asleep in this situation.

00:11:34.220 --> 00:11:35.520
It really is.

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:38.640
Well, she did do a lot for us.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:40.760
She must be tired.

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:43.720
We should sleep, too.

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:50.050
We've managed to survive to our second night.

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:54.770
I'm starting to think things
will work out somehow.

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:56.070
You think so?

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:58.130
I'm still worried.

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:01.450
Did we wake her up?

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:04.110
Papa...

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:06.020
Oh, she's just talking in her sleep is all.

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:08.780
Saying "papa." I suppose
she's got her cute points.

00:12:08.780 --> 00:12:09.790
Papa...

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:14.110
I can't eat any more b*lls...

00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:27.480
Next time, Case 3:

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:28.650
"Master of the Island."

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:29.970
<b>Master of the Island</b>
